From: tj-barrett <barrett.t@northeastern.edu>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Free the previous low-rank factor on refactorization

This fork keeps the factor in reused L/U buffers and no longer calls
coeftabExit() between numerical factorizations. Dense column blocks are fine,
but cpucblk_zalloc() reuses each compressed cblk's LRblock array and calls
core_zlralloc(..., -1, ...) on every block, which mallocs a new full-rank
buffer without freeing the previous low-rank factor. With
IPARM_COMPRESS_WHEN != Never, every refactorization (ccx: two per linear
step) leaked the whole compressed factor: 17 GB per factorization on an
829k-equation RVE, OOM after a few steps.

Free each block with core_zlrfree() before reallocating it. The array is
zeroed on first use, so this is a no-op for the first factorization.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/kernels/cpucblk_zinit.c b/kernels/cpucblk_zinit.c
index ec5adfb..32c25ab 100644
--- a/kernels/cpucblk_zinit.c
+++ b/kernels/cpucblk_zinit.c
@@ -76,12 +76,18 @@ cpucblk_zalloc( pastix_coefside_t  side,
             pastix_int_t nrows = blok_rownbr( blok );
             blok->LRblock = LRblocks;
 
+            /* A refactorization reuses the LRblock array (the coeftab is not
+             * released between factorizations): free the previous low-rank
+             * factor first, or every numerical factorization leaks it. The array
+             * is zeroed on first use, so this is a no-op then. */
             if ( side != PastixUCoef ) {
+                core_zlrfree( LRblocks );
                 core_zlralloc( nrows, ncols, -1, LRblocks );
             }
             LRblocks++;
 
             if ( side != PastixLCoef ) {
+                core_zlrfree( LRblocks );
                 core_zlralloc( nrows, ncols, -1, LRblocks );
             }
             LRblocks++;
